{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1533500-v5-setite-elder-power-feedback-needed","id":1533500,"title":"(V5) Setite elder power feedback needed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-02T16:34:24-07:00","id":1533500,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5) Setite elder power feedback needed","content":"I'm not getting more specific feedback elsewhere, so here we go here. TLDR: Ministry elder, diplomat/spy character archetype, Consensualist predator type. Longer version is she is going to be an emissary from a nearby Ministry-run city, &quot;helping&quot; the Anarchs get their shit together to overthrow the Camarilla...and/if they do, her plans are to declare herself Baron.<br /> <br /> Looking ideally for a social manipulator/seductress power selection, with lots of neat synergies. Yes, the lore relevance to the out-of-clan discipline selection is absolutely on purpose. If anyone could point out something I potentially missed or might do better, please let me know.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 4 (Cloak of Shadows, Doubletalk, Mask of a Thousand Faces, Chimerstry). Didn't opt for Vanish here, since Unseen Presence wasn't a pick (and for a reason). Chimerstry's nice and fits with the Ministry theme, but I'm not in love with it. If the character gets Obfuscate 5 later, Imposter's Guise is the clear pick. Considering swapping Doubletalk for Ventriloquism, for reasons I'll elaborate in a second.<br /> <br /> Presence 5 (Awe, Eyes of the Serpent, Lingering Kiss, True Love's Face, Majesty). Here's where the choice point between Doubletalk and Ventriloquism comes in: her level 3 pick was originally TLF and her level 4 pick was Throw Voice, before I went with Lingering Kiss and TLF. Lingering Kiss just seems more thematic given the predator type, and socially engineering short-term mortal thralls jonesing for a Kiss is 100% a Setite move (but at that point why not just take Entrancement). LK would synergize well with False Sip, if I take it as a Protean power. Given how badly Dread Gaze was nerfed in v5 and that EotS is at least comparable in terms of power/utility, big nope to that.<br /> <br /> Suffuse the Edifice could be funny, though.<br /> <br /> Protean 3 (Eyes of the Beast, Feral Weapons, Earth Meld). This one pretty much speaks for itself...but I'll be honest, the Serpent's Kiss/False Sip 1-2 punch is a metric buttload of synergy with Lingering Kiss. Might be worth it to trade Earth Meld for one of them, take the other at level 4, and finish out with Mist Form. Seems like an all-or-nothing prospect, which is why either Throw Voice or Entrancement might be better.<br /> <br /> Auspex 3 (Sense the Unseen, Premonition, Fatal Flaw). Now we're starting to get kinky. StS and Premonition speak for themselves, but the big draw for Fatal Flaw is it works in social encounters too. Scry the Soul could be just as well, but I like the Akhu-lite feel the Auspex/Oblivion amalgams bring to the table.<br /> <br /> Fortitude 3 (Resilience, Unswayable Mind, Fortify the Inner Facade). As seen elsewhere, focus here goes to the social stuff. Not really much to say, other than boy howdy is Fortitude chock full of nice powers in v5.<br /> <br /> Oblivion 2 (Shadow Cloak, Fatal Prediction). So, thanks to Shadow Cloak this character's <i>lowest</i> Stealth pool is nine dice (and that goes to twelve if blood surging), which pretty well explains the lack of Unseen Presence. Fatal Prediction is a really nice &quot;delete mortal consequence-free&quot; button, which will certainly help with &quot;unintended consequences of Presence&quot; and &quot;you have outlived your usefulness&quot; issues. Not that vampires need much help there, but being this character is a Consensualist and therefore a Masquerade-breaker...gotta tie up those loose ends if they start fraying somehow without further risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:34:51-07:00","id":1533529,"title":"","content":"It's looks like you got a solid base to work from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T16:51:59-07:00","id":1533542,"title":"","content":"It looks like you've already got everything sorted, just two tips. Shadow Perpective can be useful to install paranoia and I would advise keeping Earth Meld, most of the time you may even forget that you have this discipline considering your archetype, but it can save you in case of an emergency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T17:03:33-07:00","id":1533543,"title":"","content":"A good start you did give a solid reason why your Ministry elder has 2 dots in Oblivion and what generation is your character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T04:26:05-07:00","id":1533595,"title":"","content":"Oh, this is for an NPC in the chronicle I'm currently running. I'm just looking to give a handful of these characters funky, unorthodox power sets to make them difficult to tackle in a straightforward (for their respective clans) way. Case in point, there's a whole pack of Nosferatu in this city with the V5 variant bane, who all have Presence to some level as well as Looks merits. Started as a joke on the idea of a Siren nosferatu who uses glory holes to feed, mutated into this lore and city backstory thing, turned back into an in-joke when one of my best friends who isn't a player quipped I've created foxy Cleopatras.<br /> <br /> To be truthful I didn't even hit on the idea of approximating Akhu on this character, until I realized Oblivion does the job better than Blood Sorcery. That's a perfect lore fit given Setite-Hecata connections, having the side effect of adding a nice meaty plot hook or two -- one of the PC's is a nominally Camarilla-aligned Harbinger (and another's BH). Especially since this particular Setite is going to be more orthodox, but still very syncretic -- leaning more heavily on the gnostic aspects of Setite religion than straightforward Set worship, obsessed with the idea of shedding her mortal form and achieving theosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}